<%# "Your account" (the notes handoff's decision 25): the h1, then three
    cards -- Profile and Notes in one form with one footer, and Password, a
    form of its own with its own "Change password" footer and the promise
    about sessions directly under the card's title. The screen began as
    "Change my password" (access-control design spec §5; round 3, handoff
    "Studio Change Password"): every signed-in user's own password, behind
    their current one, plus the one profile field, their name (design pass
    spec §5.1). A deliberate submit, never autosave, like the Users module's
    own forms.

    Two forms, so two footers: each `Admin::SaveBarComponent` is the footer of
    its own form and counts only that form's changes (one Leave prompt serves
    both). The first form is the person's preferences -- the name and the two
    Notes switches (notes handoff, decision 13: preferences save the same
    way; a password change is a separate, secure step). Neither Save may
    throw away what the other form holds:
    - "Save" keeps the screen (a Turbo Stream answer, see the controller),
      so the password fields stay as typed;
    - "Change password" re-renders the screen, so it waits for the first form:
      while the name or a Notes switch is unsaved it is locked, with "Save or
      cancel your changes first." (`after:`, the D10 rule between two forms).
    The current password alone is nothing to save and is what a password
    manager fills in on load: it is not counted (`data-save-bar-ignore`), or
    every visit here would end in "Leave without saving?".
    The first form is two cards of one width (560px), Profile (the name) and
    Notes, with the one footer under both (notes handoff, decisions 19 and
    20); the Password card is 560px too, its footer under it the same way.
    Every string of the first form is a key (`admin.accounts`); the password
    form's are still literals, which is why this file is not in the i18n
    test's `CONVERTED` list. The password form is the 560px card of the mock, its footer carrying the "Forgot your
    current password?" link at the far end. The subtitle's promise is the
    service's own rule (`Users::OwnerProtection#end_sessions_after_password_
    change`: the acting session stays, the user's other sessions go). No
    typed password is ever rendered back: the inputs have no `value`. %>
<% content_for :title, t("admin.accounts.title") %>
<% field_errors = @field_errors || {} %>
<div class="max-w-[560px]">
  <h1 class="mb-4 text-h1 text-ink"><%= t("admin.accounts.title") %></h1>

  <%# One summary at a time: only one of the two forms was submitted. The
      password form's messages link to their fields; the service's own
      sentences stand when it left no per-field errors (a denial). %>
  <%= render Admin::ErrorSummaryComponent.new(errors: field_errors.presence || Array(@errors),
        field_ids: { current_password: "current_password", password: "password", password_confirmation: "password_confirmation" }) %>
  <%= render Admin::ErrorSummaryComponent.new(errors: Array(@profile_errors)) %>

  <%# What the form shows: the account as stored, or, after a refusal, what
      was sent (`@profile_values`, see the controller). %>
  <% profile = @profile_values || { name: Current.user.name, notes_sound: Current.user.notes_sound, notes_desktop: Current.user.notes_desktop } %>
  <%= form_with url: admin_account_profile_path(**admin_url_options), method: :patch, id: "profile-form", class: "mb-8",
        data: save_bar_form_data(dirty: Array(@profile_errors).any?) do %>
    <section class="mb-4 max-w-[560px] rounded-cs border border-line bg-surface" aria-labelledby="account-profile">
      <div class="border-b border-line px-[18px] py-3.5">
        <h3 id="account-profile" class="text-base font-semibold text-ink"><%= t("admin.accounts.profile.title") %></h3>
      </div>
      <div class="px-[18px] py-3.5">
        <%= label_tag "name", t("admin.accounts.profile.name"), class: setup_label_class %>
        <%= text_field_tag "name", profile[:name], id: "name", maxlength: 120, autocomplete: "name", class: setup_input_class %>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%# Notes (notes spec §6.4, D18, D19; handoff "Account switches" and
        decisions 13-16): two settings of the person's, saved with this
        form's footer like any configuration -- never autosaved, never
        through the write queue. A hidden "0" ahead of each box makes an
        unticked switch submit; `admin--save-bar` does not count a hidden
        input, so the box alone is.

        The SETTING is the person's and follows them to every browser; the
        PERMISSION to notify is this browser's. The lines under the second
        switch are about the permission and are shown ONLY WHILE THAT SWITCH
        IS ON -- as it stands in the page, saved or not: turning it on shows
        the line at once (`admin--notes-permission`, which holds the switch
        as its target). Not asked yet: the accent-toned info line with
        "Allow in this browser", which asks at once, in the click, outside
        the save -- the button is `type="button"` with no name, so it is no
        field of the form and is never locked by it. Allowed: nothing.
        Blocked: the warn-toned sentence, no button. Both lines are drawn
        hidden and the script shows the one that applies. The permission is
        changed in the browser's own settings too, so it is read again
        whenever the window is looked at again. %>
    <section class="max-w-[560px] rounded-cs border border-line bg-surface" aria-labelledby="account-notes">
      <div class="border-b border-line px-[18px] py-3.5">
        <h3 id="account-notes" class="text-base font-semibold text-ink"><%= t("admin.accounts.notes.title") %></h3>
        <p class="text-[13px] text-dim"><%= t("admin.accounts.notes.description") %></p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-b border-line px-[18px] py-3.5">
        <label class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm text-ink">
          <span><%= t("admin.accounts.notes.notes_sound") %></span>
          <%= hidden_field_tag "notes_sound", "0", id: nil %>
          <%= check_box_tag "notes_sound", "1", profile[:notes_sound], role: "switch", class: "cs-toggle" %>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="px-[18px] py-3.5" data-controller="admin--notes-permission" data-state="unsupported"
           data-action="visibilitychange@document->admin--notes-permission#render focus@window->admin--notes-permission#render">
        <label class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm text-ink">
          <span><%= t("admin.accounts.notes.notes_desktop") %></span>
          <%= hidden_field_tag "notes_desktop", "0", id: nil %>
          <%= check_box_tag "notes_desktop", "1", profile[:notes_desktop], role: "switch", class: "cs-toggle",
                data: { "admin--notes-permission-target": "switch", action: "change->admin--notes-permission#render" } %>
        </label>
        <div role="status">
          <div class="mt-2 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 rounded-cs bg-accent-tint px-3 py-2.5 text-[13px] text-ink" data-admin--notes-permission-target="ask" hidden>
            <span><%= t("admin.accounts.notes.permission.ask") %></span>
            <%= render Admin::ButtonComponent.new(label: t("admin.accounts.notes.permission.allow"), variant: :secondary, size: :small, type: "button",
                  class: "shrink-0", data: { action: "admin--notes-permission#allow" }) %>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-2 rounded-cs border border-warn bg-warn-tint px-3 py-2.5 text-[13px] text-ink" data-admin--notes-permission-target="blocked" hidden><%= t("admin.accounts.notes.permission.blocked") %></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%= render Admin::SaveBarComponent.new(form_id: "profile-form", cancel_url: admin_root_path(**admin_url_options), save_label: t("admin.accounts.save")) %>
  <% end %>

  <%= form_with url: admin_account_password_path(**admin_url_options), method: :patch, id: "password-form", data: save_bar_form_data(dirty: Array(@errors).any?, after: "profile-form") do %>
    <section class="max-w-[560px] rounded-cs border border-line bg-surface" aria-labelledby="account-password">
      <div class="border-b border-line px-[18px] py-3.5">
        <h3 id="account-password" class="text-base font-semibold text-ink"><%= t("admin.accounts.password.title") %></h3>
        <p class="text-[13px] text-dim"><%= t("admin.accounts.password.sessions") %></p>
      </div>
      <div class="px-[18px] pt-3.5">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <%= render Admin::PasswordFieldComponent.new(name: "current_password", id: "current_password", label: "Current password",
                autocomplete: "current-password", autofocus: true, errors: field_errors[:current_password], "data-save-bar-ignore": true) %>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-4">
          <%= render Admin::PasswordFieldComponent.new(name: "password", id: "password", label: "New password", meter: true, errors: field_errors[:password]) %>
        </div>

        <div class="mb-4">
          <%= render Admin::PasswordFieldComponent.new(name: "password_confirmation", id: "password_confirmation", label: "Confirm new password",
                errors: field_errors[:password_confirmation]) %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%= render Admin::SaveBarComponent.new(form_id: "password-form", cancel_url: admin_root_path(**admin_url_options), save_label: "Change password", save_data: { password_submit: true }) do %>
      <%# The reset flow is public and signs nobody out by being visited; it
          asks for an email, so it is only useful where mail is configured
          (System status says when it isn't). Opened in the page, not the
          frame: it is a different layout. %>
      <%= link_to "Forgot your current password?", new_admin_password_path, data: { turbo_frame: "_top" }, class: "text-[13px] text-accent hover:text-accent-hover hover:underline" %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
